-- title:
--   Single-place shift by s on the quaternionic class set
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$ and write $\mathbb{H} = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ for the associated quaternion algebra. Let $O \subseteq \mathbb{H}$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11), i.e. it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and is finitely generated. Let $q$ be a prime and $v$ a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q \in v$. Let $s \in \mathbb{H}^{\times}$ and let $s_f$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H} \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ whose image under base-changed evaluation at $u$ equals $s \otimes 1$ for every height-one prime $u$ with $q \notin u$, and equals $1$ for every $u$ with $q \in u$. Let $x,y$ be units of $\mathbb{H} \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ whose components at every $u \neq v$ are $1$, and suppose the $v$-component of $y$ equals the product of the $v$-component of the inverse of the diagonal image of $s$ with the $v$-component of $x$. Then $y$ and $x s_f$ have the same class in the double coset quotient of $(\mathbb{H} \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f})^{\times}$ by the range of the diagonal embedding $\mathbb{H}^{\times} \to (\mathbb{H} \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f})^{\times}$ on the left and, on the right, by the stabiliser in $(\mathbb{H} \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f})^{\times}$ of the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z \otimes \alpha$ with $z \in O$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere-integral finite adele.
--
--   This is the class-set counterpart of the shift map in the Čerednik–Drinfeld dictionary: left translation by $s^{-1}$ at the single place $v$ agrees, on double cosets, with right translation by the idele of $s$ truncated away from the places above $q$, and no local integrality or unit condition on $s$ at $v$ is imposed. It is used in the identification of the coset graph attached to a Mumford-side frame with the class set, and in the comparison of class-set classes with their shifted counterparts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_classSet_mk_eq_mk_mul_of_finiteAdeleEvalAt_eq_inv_mul.lean

